  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "While we're glad VRC are at least trying to give us official versions of the mods we've come to know and love, we have an idea to balance the scales between the dev-team and consumers; it would be soo much easier if they implemented a mod-approval scheme where people can submit mods for review to be approved by VRC themselves. That way, they get EAC and control over what mods do or don't get sent packing- and we get to use the good wholesome mods we love.\nBy having the VRC team approve or deny mods, they gain control over what they deem harmful or not, and we the community get to continue enjoying the mods that help bring us together, add accessibility, provide tools for vrchat content creators, optimize the game, and soo much more. In addition to this, it could make modded features safer and more accessible to those who would like to use them, but don't know how.",
